        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2005",
        "question_text": "<p>If $\\sin \\theta = \\frac{3}{5}$, find $\\cos \\theta$ given that $\\theta$ is acute.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Using the Pythagorean identity, $\\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^2 \\theta = 1$. Thus, $\\cos^2 \\theta = 1 - \\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)^2 = 1 - \\frac{9}{25} = \\frac{16}{25}$. Therefore, $\\cos \\theta = \\frac{4}{5}$ since $\\theta$ is acute.</p>",
